\]

which is compact by Arzelà–Ascoli, and prove that the required subset is invariant. Then explain whether the persistence theorem applies to this set as a manifold or only supports a Lipschitz graph/fixed-point argument.

#### Route C: noncompact bounded-geometry theorem

If using a noncompact normally hyperbolic manifold, state the bounded-geometry and uniformity hypotheses required by the exact theorem. Verify them; do not merely cite a noncompact extension.

